1
00:00:04,442 --> 00:00:09,031
Whiskers and Luna's World. Episode three. The Five Oceans!

2
00:00:15,894 --> 00:00:19,893
Luna, why is your globe so blue? Did it fall in the bath?

3
00:00:20,093 --> 00:00:21,690
Blue means water, Whiskers!

4
00:00:21,890 --> 00:00:24,292
And all that water is in five big oceans.

5
00:00:27,268 --> 00:00:29,540
Five oceans? Let's go and see them all!

6
00:00:29,740 --> 00:00:31,126
Hold on to the cushion!

7
00:00:40,764 --> 00:00:42,983
Up into space they flew!

8
00:00:46,514 --> 00:00:51,173
This giant one is the Pacific Ocean. The biggest and deepest ocean of all!

9
00:00:51,373 --> 00:00:53,267
It covers almost half the world!

10
00:00:57,908 --> 00:01:00,683
Next, the Atlantic Ocean, the second biggest.

11
00:01:04,769 --> 00:01:06,652
Here is the warm Indian Ocean.

12
00:01:10,738 --> 00:01:14,566
At the top, the Arctic Ocean. The smallest, and often frozen.

13
00:01:18,653 --> 00:01:22,208
At the bottom, the cold Southern Ocean, around Antarctica.

14
00:01:25,184 --> 00:01:28,445
Pacific, Atlantic, Indian, Arctic, Southern. Five!

15
00:01:35,863 --> 00:01:38,903
And they're all joined up, like one big world ocean!

16
00:01:39,103 --> 00:01:42,434
I vote for the biggest one. More room for napping.

17
00:01:54,848 --> 00:01:58,202
They landed in the middle of the Pacific Ocean.

18
00:02:02,844 --> 00:02:04,569
What's that beautiful singing?

19
00:02:09,211 --> 00:02:12,066
Hellooo, little ones. I'm Bluebell, a blue whale.

20
00:02:12,266 --> 00:02:16,232
The biggest animal that ever lived. Even bigger than the dinosaurs!

21
00:02:20,873 --> 00:02:24,902
All this flying made me thirsty. A whole ocean to drink!

22
00:02:29,543 --> 00:02:32,254
Bleh! Salty! Who put salt in the sea?

23
00:02:34,952 --> 00:02:37,804
Sea water is salty, Whiskers. Here is why.

24
00:02:38,004 --> 00:02:42,602
Rain washes tiny bits of salt out of rocks, and rivers carry it to the sea.

25
00:02:42,802 --> 00:02:47,101
The sun lifts the water up into the clouds, but the salt stays behind.

26
00:02:52,853 --> 00:02:56,220
I knew that. I tasted it on purpose. For science.

27
00:03:02,250 --> 00:03:03,866
Whoa! What makes the waves?

28
00:03:04,066 --> 00:03:07,361
The wind! It blows over the water and pushes it into bumps.

29
00:03:12,558 --> 00:03:14,558
Come and see my deep, deep home.

30
00:03:23,641 --> 00:03:27,292
In a magic bubble, they sank down, down, down.

31
00:03:31,933 --> 00:03:33,684
It's getting darker and darker!

32
00:03:33,884 --> 00:03:38,921
The Pacific is so deep, its deepest place is deeper than the tallest mountain is high!

33
00:03:45,783 --> 00:03:47,716
Look, a fish with its own lamp!

34
00:03:47,916 --> 00:03:51,016
Ooh. A fish with a night light. Very cosy.

35
00:04:00,099 --> 00:04:03,321
That evening, they landed on a quiet beach.

36
00:04:03,521 --> 00:04:05,468
Hey! Watch your step! That's my rock pool!

37
00:04:05,668 --> 00:04:07,747
Sorry! Why is the sea so far out?

38
00:04:07,947 --> 00:04:11,249
It's the tide! Twice a day the sea comes in, and goes out again.

39
00:04:18,667 --> 00:04:20,319
What pulls all that water?

40
00:04:20,519 --> 00:04:23,095
The Moon! It pulls the sea, like a gentle magnet.

41
00:04:29,402 --> 00:04:32,948
The Moon? I once chased a Moon Fish. It got away.

42
00:04:41,754 --> 00:04:44,733
Remember! One. There are five oceans.

43
00:04:47,432 --> 00:04:51,400
Two. The Pacific is the biggest and the deepest ocean.

44
00:04:54,098 --> 00:04:56,443
Three. Sea water is salty.

45
00:05:02,751 --> 00:05:07,589
Quiz time! Which ocean is the biggest? The Atlantic, or the Pacific?

46
00:05:10,565 --> 00:05:12,609
The Pacific! Well done!

47
00:05:15,030 --> 00:05:18,012
Next. Is sea water salty, or sweet?

48
00:05:20,988 --> 00:05:24,067
Salty! Don't drink it, like Whiskers did!

49
00:05:30,929 --> 00:05:33,644
And with a twinkle, they were home again.

50
00:05:33,844 --> 00:05:36,606
Ahh. My water bowl. Not salty at all.

51
00:05:36,806 --> 00:05:39,409
Goodnight, Bluebell. Goodnight, five oceans!

52
00:05:42,940 --> 00:05:47,582
Next time, mountains and volcanoes! Goodnight, big blue world.

